A||N||5||FieroGT 914||Starter / Electrical Problems...||||5||
Z||000000||FieroGT 914||06-27-2001||09:46 AM||||i got in my 86GT to drive home last night and the darn thing wouldn't start!  there was a clicking noise and the lights dimmed.  i let the car sit for about 5 minutes and then tried again and it started right up.  deciding not to take anymore chances, i went right home and parked it - it made it but i tried to start it immediately after turning it off and got the same clicking problem with the lights dimming once again.  any ideas on what may be wrong??? i will be investigating it more after work today but i wanted to get some input on where to start if anyone else had the same problem before.  i think the starter may not be engaging properly but it's just a guess right now.  any help is greatly appreciated! thanks!<P>P.S. Is anyone going to the All GM Nationals at Carlisle this weekend???<P>------------------------<BR>Joe<BR>-White 86 GT<BR>-Just purchased Maroon 87 GT||||reg||5
Z||000001||isthiswhereiputausername?||06-27-2001||09:56 AM||||Sounds like a loose starter wire||||reg||1
Z||000002||SteveJ||06-27-2001||09:59 AM||||Sounds like the classical GM starter problem. It get hot and the resistance increases to the point where it won't work but as soon as it cools it works fine. Lots of people put heat shields around their starters to reduce the problem. Apparently it cranked fine when it cooled so its not the battery. Just get a rebuilt starter.||||reg||1
Z||000003||SteveJ||06-27-2001||10:01 AM||||Nope not a loose wire. The lights dimmed. That's a big current drain so the power went into the starter, it just didn't do anything.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Voytek||06-27-2001||06:40 PM||||Check the positive / negative wire on the battery.  A shop left mine kinda loose one time and it was doing the exact thing.  I think it's especially the red wire - the current during cranking is high enough to actually push it away from the battery.  Sometimes it will go, sometimes it will not.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/voyteks_sig2.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||FieroGT 914||06-28-2001||09:01 AM||||thanks guys... i took everything apart last night - lemme tell ya, it would've been nice to have a car lift instead of laying on my back all night but i think i got the problem fixed.  all of the connections were solid and everything looked fine mechanically.  my best guess is that it overheated.  nevertheless, i took the starter soleniod apart and some of it seemed like it was starting to corrode a bit.  it wasn't bad, but i went to the parts store and bought a new one.  everything works great so far.  we'll see what happens when the car gets hot though so i'm keeping my fingers crossed. thanks!||||reg||1
